[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605263803-biomethane-d-gate-evaluation-r0", :adr/title "Biomethane from anaerobic digestion of agricultural waste — D1..D5 evaluation R0 (sub-ADR of 2605263500; closes turquoise H₂ §3 deferral of 2605263600)", :adr/status "proposed-pending-council-ratification", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605263803: Biomethane from anaerobic digestion — D1..D5 evaluation R0\n\n**Status**: proposed-pending-council-ratification\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (Founder, Seat 1) — pending Council Lv7+ unanimity cascade from ADR-2605263500\n**Constitutional weight**: sub-evaluation under D1..D5 framework\n\n# Context\n\nADR-2605263600 §3 (turquoise hydrogen) deferred conditional on religious-corp closed-loop biomethane source. This ADR provides that source.\n\nBiomethane = CH₄ upgraded from biogas (50-70% CH₄ + 30-50% CO₂ + trace H₂S/NH₃/siloxanes) produced via mesophilic / thermophilic anaerobic digestion (AD) of organic waste. Carbon is biogenic short-cycle (from photosynthesis within prior 1-10 years → biomass → AD → CH₄ → combustion → atmospheric CO₂ → photosynthesis), closed-loop.\n\n| Feedstock | Source actor | Yield (Nm³ CH₄/t VS) | Religious-corp availability |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Crop residue (straw, husks) | mitsuho R1+ | 200-300 | Moderate (cellulosic, slower digestion) |\n| Livestock manure | mitsuho R2+ livestock | 200-400 | High (mesophilic, easy) |\n| Food scraps | mitsuho + iyashi/hagukumi/manabi facilities | 400-600 | High (energy-dense, fast) |\n| Sewage sludge (biosolids) | mizuho R2+ wastewater | 250-350 | High (mizuho infrastructure pair) |\n| Industrial organic (hodoki ELV lubricants — NOT included) | hodoki | n/a | Excluded — contamination risk to soil-applied digestate |\n| Energy crops (corn silage / sorghum) | (NONE — N4 of hikari R0 food-crop biofuel ban) | n/a | **Prohibited** (N4) |\n\n# Decision\n\n## §1 AD biomethane from organic waste — CONDITIONALLY PERMITTED\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | ✓ Feedstock from religious-corp internal waste streams (mitsuho / mizuho / hodoki / facilities); digester + upgrading equipment religious-corp-owned open-hardware |\n| **D2** | ✓ Digestate (residual liquid + solid) is short-cycle biological matter; soil-applied per N4 mitsuho carve-out below |\n| **D3** | ✓ Closed-loop carbon: CO₂ released by combustion = same CO₂ fixed by photosynthesis within 1-10 yr. AD CO₂ stripped during upgrading can be vented to atmosphere (re-fixed by photosynthesis) OR captured for downstream use (algae bioreactor for §2.2 of 2605263500 microbial hydrocarbon, or beverage-grade CO₂ for greenhouse mitsuho fertilization, etc.) — both pathways net-zero or net-negative |\n| **D4** | ✓ No fissile material |\n| **D5** | ✓ Digester + biogas upgrading (PSA / water-scrubbing / amine-scrubbing / membrane-separation) + control firmware Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider |\n\n**Verdict**: PERMITTED under the following operational conditions:\n\n1. **Feedstock provenance**: every batch carries `com.etzhayyim.hikari.biomethaneFeedstockAttestation` Lexicon entry listing source actor + waste-stream-CID + dry-matter mass + VS (volatile solids) mass; energy-crop feedstock (corn / sorghum / sugarcane for biogas) **categorically excluded** per N4 of hikari R0\n2. **No municipal-waste accept**: biomethane plant MUST NOT accept commercial municipal organic waste contracts (D1 — vendor dependency + contamination tracing burden). Internal religious-corp streams only.\n3. **Digester open-hardware**: continuously-stirred tank reactor (CSTR) OR plug-flow OR covered lagoon; mechanical design + control firmware Apache 2.0 + Rider per D5. Stainless steel pressure vessel + biogas membrane gasholder + heating loop heat-recovery from upgrading\n4. **Upgrading technology**: PSA / water-scrubbing / amine-scrubbing / membrane-separation all permitted; vendor IP-encumbered upgrading skids (e.g., proprietary water-scrubbing controllers) require open-firmware retrofit before commissioning\n5. **CH₄ leak rate ≤1%**: CH₄ is GWP100 ~28-34 per IPCC AR6 WG1; per-facility quarterly Optical Gas Imaging (OGI) leak survey + repair-or-shutdown ≤30 days\n6. **Storage limits R0-R3**:\n   - Per LANDS.md parcel: ≤500 Nm³ biomethane stored at any time (gasholder + low-pressure CNG cylinders ≤200 bar)\n   - Religious-corp aggregate: ≤2,000 Nm³ biomethane stored total\n7. **Use priority order**: (a) on-site heat/CHP for digester + upgrading auto-consumption + adjacent facility heat; (b) pipeline injection — **PROHIBITED through R3** (would create commercial gas-grid dependency D1); (c) compressed-NG vehicle fuel — wadachi R3+ separately; (d) turquoise H₂ pyrolysis feedstock per ADR-2605263600 §3 (R2+ if H₂ pathway active); (e) green NH₃ feedstock via SMR equivalent — **PROHIBITED** (would re-introduce SMR pathway; green NH₃ MUST use green H₂ per 2605263700)\n8. **Digestate routing**: liquid digestate + solids → mitsuho compost cell as fertilizer-N alternative per 2605263700 §4 priority order (tertiary \"compost-derived N\"); chigiri cross-actor verification of N content + heavy-metal screen + pathogen kill (mesophilic ≥30 days OR thermophilic ≥15 days OR Class A biosolids pasteurization)\n9. **Annual review**: `silenBiomethaneReview` Council Lv6+ ≥3: feedstock-CID chain, zero-municipal-contract, leak rate, digestate-to-mitsuho mass balance\n\n## §2 Landfill gas + sewage-gas-fired turbine — PROHIBITED\n\n| Source | Failing gate |\n|---|---|\n| Commercial landfill gas | D1 (commercial waste industry dependency) |\n| Municipal sewage treatment plant CHP (third-party operator) | D1 (commercial utility dependency) |\n\nReligious-corp mizuho R2+ owns its own biosolids → AD permitted under §1; commercial landfill / municipal sewage are not.\n\n## §3 Energy-crop biogas — ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED\n\nInherits hikari R0 N4 (no biofuel from food crops). Corn silage / sorghum / sugarcane / energy-grass dedicated cropping for AD feedstock displaces food production — same multi-gen invariant as N4.\n\n## §4 Cross-actor mesh\n\n| Actor | Role | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| **mitsuho** R2+ | Crop residue + livestock manure + food scrap feedstock upstream | → biomethane plant |\n| **mitsuho** R2+ | Digestate as fertilizer-N (compost-derived priority) | ← biomethane plant |\n| **hodoki** R2+ | Organic ELV residuals — **EXCLUDED** per §1 contamination risk | (none) |\n| **mizuho** R2+ | Biosolids feedstock upstream + treated effluent for digester make-up water | → biomethane plant |\n| **iyashi / hagukumi / manabi** R1+ | Food scrap feedstock from facility kitchens | → biomethane plant |\n| **hikari** R2+ | Heat / CHP power consumer of biomethane | ← biomethane plant |\n| **hydrogen** R2+ (ADR-2605263600 §3 turquoise pathway) | Biomethane → CH₄ pyrolysis → H₂ + solid C feedstock | ← biomethane plant |\n| **wadachi** R3+ | Compressed biomethane vehicle fuel pilot (separate ADR) | ← biomethane plant |\n| **chigiri** R1+ | Digestate cross-actor verification + cross-jurisdiction permit | (verification) |\n| **toritate** R1+ | Public Fund accounting for biomethane CHP revenue → Public Fund | (audit) |\n\n## §5 Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Date / Trigger | Scope | Cap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | this commit | This ADR + path-reserved `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-hikari/cells/biomethane_anaerobic_digester/` import-time RuntimeError | None |\n| **R1** | post-Council ratification of 2605263500 + this ADR + mitsuho R1 livestock attested OR mizuho R1 biosolids attested | Single ≤50 Nm³/day CSTR digester + ≤200 Nm³ low-pressure gasholder + no upgrading (use raw biogas for on-site heat only) | 50 Nm³/day biogas |\n| **R2** | post-R1 + ≥1 anaerobic-digestion-engineer on Council + 1-year safe operation | ≤100 Nm³/day + PSA upgrading to biomethane ≥95% CH₄ + ≤200 Nm³ biomethane storage | 100 Nm³/day biomethane |\n| **R3** | post-R2 + 30-day public + cross-actor mitsuho compost-N integration | ≤200 Nm³/day religious-corp aggregate + ≤500 Nm³/parcel + activates turquoise H₂ §3 pathway (ADR-2605263600) | 200 Nm³/day |\n\n## §6 New Lexicons\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.hikari.{\n  biomethaneFeedstockAttestation,    # per-batch: source actor + waste-stream CID + VS mass + retention time\n  biomethaneProductionAttestation,   # per-Nm³: digester ID + CH₄ % + upgrading method + leak survey date\n  biomethaneStorageInventory,        # per-LANDS-parcel: Nm³ current + pressure + gasholder type\n  digestateRoutingAttestation,       # per-batch: mitsuho parcel + N-P-K + heavy-metal screen + pathogen kill\n  silenBiomethaneReview              # annual Council Lv6+ ≥3: feedstock chain + leak rate + digestate balance\n}\n```\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**:\n- Closes turquoise H₂ deferral from ADR-2605263600 §3 (religious-corp can now access turquoise H₂ pathway via this ADR's biomethane R3)\n- Cross-actor waste-stream valorization: turns mitsuho + mizuho + facility waste from disposal cost to energy + fertilizer asset\n- Digestate as fertilizer-N hedges mitsuho 2605263700 §4 tertiary-priority N source\n- Net-zero or net-negative carbon at facility level (if AD CO₂ captured for algae or greenhouse fertilization)\n\n**Negative**:\n- Capex ~$3,000-8,000 per Nm³/day biomethane capacity (R1 ≤50 Nm³/day = ~$150-400K)\n- Digester upset risk (acidification / foaming / inhibition by NH₃ at high livestock manure loading); operator training burden\n- Sulfide (H₂S) corrosion risk in upstream piping; biological / chemical desulfurization mandatory\n- Slow throughput: AD retention time 20-40 days mesophilic OR 12-20 days thermophilic; energy yield modest vs solar\n- Pathogen kill protocol burden for Class A biosolids equivalent + helminth-ovum monitoring (mizuho cross-actor)\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n- **Defer biomethane until R3**: rejected — closes 2605263600 §3 turquoise deferral and provides upstream feedstock for that pathway; sequencing benefits from co-ratification\n- **Permit commercial landfill-gas off-take**: rejected — D1 commercial waste-industry dependency; landfill methane recovery is a commercial industry with vendor lock-in\n- **Permit energy-crop dedicated biogas**: rejected — N4 food-crop displacement\n- **Pipeline-inject biomethane to public gas grid**: rejected through R3 — D1 commercial gas-grid dependency; on-site combustion or H₂-pyrolysis only\n\n# Open Questions\n\n1. **Digester technology R1**: CSTR (most flexible, good for liquid feedstock) vs plug-flow (better for high-solids feedstock) vs covered lagoon (cheapest, slow). To be decided at R1 ADR based on initial feedstock mix.\n2. **Upgrading technology R2**: PSA (mature, modest cost) vs water-scrubbing (simplest, water-intensive) vs membrane (compact, higher cost). Likely PSA.\n3. **Digestate de-watering technology**: belt-press vs screw-press vs centrifuge — open-hardware survey needed.\n4. **wadachi CNG-biomethane vehicle pilot**: separate ADR at wadachi R3+.\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605263500 (parent D1..D5)\n- ADR-2605263600 (hydrogen — §3 turquoise pathway closed by this ADR §1.7(d))\n- ADR-2605263700 (ammonia — §4 digestate as tertiary N source)\n- ADR-2605261015 (mitsuho — feedstock + digestate consumer)\n- ADR-2605263100 (mizuho — biosolids feedstock + makeup water)\n- ADR-2605261215 (hodoki — organic ELV explicitly excluded §1)\n- IPCC AR6 WG1 — CH₄ GWP100 reference\n- ISO 17225 — Biofuel feedstock classification (referenced for §1.1 attestation)\n- Class A biosolids — US EPA 40 CFR 503 (referenced for §1.8 pathogen kill)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605263803-biomethane-d-gate-evaluation-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "biomethane-d-gate-evaluation", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26", :adr/date "2026-05-26", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605263700-green-ammonia-d-gate-evaluation-r0"], :adr/authoritative_for ["Anaerobic digestion biomethane D1..D5 evaluation" "Biomethane conditional permit (≤200 Nm³/day religious-corp aggregate R3; storage ≤500 Nm³ per LANDS parcel R3)" "Cross-actor feedstock waste-stream routing (mitsuho food/crop residue + hodoki ELV organic + mizuho biosolids + livestock manure)" "Turquoise H₂ pathway activation conditional permit (closes ADR-2605263600 §3 deferral)" "Digestate routing to mitsuho compost as fertilizer-N alternative"]}]
